### Component 2: AI Evaluation Module ([ai.py](file:///d:/sem6/Computer%20EngeLab/SmartScribe/backend/ai.py) + `/api/evaluate`)

**Responsibility:** Takes essay title and content, calls the OpenRouter LLM API, and returns structured scores (Grammar, Coherence, Argumentation) plus textual feedback.

**Key Implementation — [ai.py](file:///d:/sem6/Computer%20EngeLab/SmartScribe/backend/ai.py):**
```python
from openai import OpenAI   # OpenAI-compatible client for OpenRouter

def get_ai_evaluation(title, content):
    client = OpenAI(
        base_url="https://openrouter.ai/api/v1",
        api_key=OPENROUTER_API_KEY,
    )
    prompt = f"""You are an expert essay grader. Evaluate the following essay.
Title: {title}
Content: {content}

Provide three scores (0-100) and feedback. Output EXACTLY as valid JSON:
{{ "grammar": 85, "coherence": 78, "argumentation": 92, "feedback": "..." }}
"""
    response = client.chat.completions.create(
        model="openrouter/auto",
        messages=[{"role": "user", "content": prompt}],
    )
    text = response.choices[0].message.content
    res = json.loads(re.search(r'\{.*\}', text, re.DOTALL).group(0))
    overall = round((res["grammar"] + res["coherence"] + res["argumentation"]) / 3, 1)
    return {...res, "overall": overall}
```

**Key Implementation — Evaluation Route ([main.py](file:///d:/sem6/Computer%20EngeLab/SmartScribe/backend/main.py)):**
```python
@app.post("/api/evaluate")
async def evaluate_essay(
    essay: EssaySubmit,
    user_id: int = Depends(auth.get_current_user_id)   # JWT validation
):
    result = ai.get_ai_evaluation(essay.title, essay.content)  # AI call
    
    db.save_essay(                              # Persist to database
        user_id=user_id,
        title=essay.title,
        content=essay.content,
        grammar=result["grammar"],
        coherence=result["coherence"],
        argument=result["argumentation"],
        overall=result["overall"],
        feedback=result["feedback"]
    )
    return result
```

**Interaction with other components:**
- **Auth Module** (`auth.get_current_user_id`) validates the JWT before evaluation is allowed.
- **Database Module** (`db.save_essay`) persists results so the Dashboard can retrieve history.
- **OpenRouter External API** is called to perform actual LLM inference.
- **Frontend Evaluate View** (`Evaluate.jsx`) sends the essay and renders the returned score cards.

